ers/limotova/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/limotova/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/limotova/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/comments/3810066190","html_url":"https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/141379#issuecomment-3810066190","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/141379","id":3810066190,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAAe_f87jGP8O","user":{"login":"craigtaverner","id":114451,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNDQ1MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/114451?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/craigtaverner","html_url":"https://github.com/craigtaverner","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/craigtaverner/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/craigtaverner/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/craigtaverner/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/craigtaverner/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/craigtaverner/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/craigtaverner/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/craigtaverner/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/craigtaverner/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/craigtaverner/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-28T09:28:04Z","updated_at":"2026-01-28T09:28:04Z","body":"I was also thinking that the current format for original_types is insufficient, because it does not include the time_series_metric, which in this case is the key reason for the incompatibility. Right now original_types looks like:\n```\n\"original_types\": [\n  \"double\",\n  \"keyword\"\n]\n```\n\nAnd that makes sense when it is just the DataType that clashes, but when it is two doubles, one a gauge and the other a counter, this does not make sense. We need an expanded format, perhaps:\n```\n\"original_types\": [\n  {\"type\": \"double\", \"time_series_metric\": \"gauge\"},\n  {\"type\": \"double\", \"time_series_metric\": \"counter\"}\n]\n```\n\nAnd Kibana needs to be updated to cope with the type being either a string `\"double\"` or an object `{\"type\": \"double\"}`, possibly with additional information: `{\"type\": \"double\", \"time_series_metric\": \"gauge\"}` ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/comments/3810066190/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"craigtaverner","id":114451,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNDQ1MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/114451?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/craigtaverner","html_url":"https://github.com/craigtaverner","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/craigtaverner/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/craigtaverner/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/craigtaverner/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/craigtaverner/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/craigtaverner/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/craigtaverner/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/craigtaverner/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/craigtaverner/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/craigtaverner/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":22342947041,"node_id":"SE_lADOAAe_f87mLCPEzwAAAAUzvlDh","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/events/22342947041","actor":{"login":"miguel-